    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.4. Increased capacity of ILO constituents to strengthen legislation, polices and measures to ensure equal opportunities and treatment in the world of work for persons with disabilities and other persons in vulnerable situations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.The VCT@WORK Initiative was implemented (from May 2020, to August 2021) to mobilize young men and women (including people living with disabilities and people in the informal sector) to access HIV testing (and self-testing). A total number of 13,756 men and women (6,680 women and 7076 men) were counselled, tested and received result with Rapid Diagnostic Test Kits and HIV Self-Test kits.  This initiative did allow the identification of 62 positive cases (38 W &amp; 24 M) that were referred to appropriate health services for follow-up  

2.A behavior change communication apparatus for Workplace prevention and control for COVID- 19 was implemented (from June  3rd  2020, to June 5th2021) and other health related issues. This initiative benefited 300 men and woman; including people living with disabilities. The initiative aimed at ensuring equal opportunities and treatment through economic empowerment with a view to support treatment adherence in the context of COVID-19  

3.An HIV self-testing pilot initiative was implemented in May 2021 through the capacity development of HIV workplace peer educators in Lagos, Abuja, Akwa Ibom. This initiative benefited 30 workplace focal persons. 1.For the VCT@Work initiative, ILO provided (in May 2021) financial, technical and normative support.  

2.For the behaviour change communication apparatus, ILO provided (in June 2021) technical and financial support, as well as resource person.  

3.For the HIV self-testing pilot initiative, ILO provided financial and technical support as well as HIV self-test kits and capacity building for 30 pilot resource persons.</narrative>
   </description>
